[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   Closing probes on the frame-anchored bipolar reading of steps
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   129-132.
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   T1  Axisymmetric harmonic power: the per-era kick-regressed residual
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   is expanded in Legendre modes (l = 1, 2, 3) of the bipolar polar
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   angle.  A bipolar field should put its leading power in l = 1
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   with opposite signs across eras.  Extremeness of each era's l = 1
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   amplitude is priced by residual shuffle.
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   T2  Free-dipole mirror pair: the residual-weighted dipole vector is
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   fitted freely per era (no declared direction).  The joint
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   mirror-pair statistic -- deviation of the two bipolar polar
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   angles from supplementary plus the azimuth separation -- is
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   compared against within-era shuffles that preserve the coverage
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   geometry.
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   T3  ISO meridian ledger: bipolar-frame (theta, phi) of every leg of
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   the three interstellar objects (arrival, periapsis, departure)
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   against the measured meridian plane and cone band.  Descriptive
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   plus binomial occupancy -- n = 9 leg directions, so weight is
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   registered as a ledger datum, not a detection.
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   T4  Resident radial-gradient control: per-object bipolar cone angle
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   of the detached-resident varpi directions versus perihelion
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   distance.  The nested detachment-cell map shows a cone gradient;
[2026-09-21 15:17:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 133]   this tests whether it survives at per-object level.
